// Release and archive builds: Duo Streaks v2 is never compiled in by default, and unlike
// `Duo.xcconfig` this file does not include `Duo.local.xcconfig`, so a gitignored file left
// in a worktree for Xcode's Run button cannot put Duo into a build that goes to TestFlight.
// A release that ships Duo says so on purpose, on the command line:
// `DUO_V2_CONDITION=DUO_V2`.
DUO_V2_CONDITION =
// The app signs with `$(DUO_ENTITLEMENTS)` (project.yml), so Release needs the plain file here
// too: left unset it is empty, and an archive would be signed with no entitlements at all, no
// push, iCloud or HealthKit. A Duo archive also passes
// `DUO_ENTITLEMENTS=HydroDrop/HydroDrop.duo.entitlements`, which adds App Attest;
// `DUO_V2=1 Scripts/release.sh archive` passes both.
DUO_ENTITLEMENTS = HydroDrop/HydroDrop.entitlements
